  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nQuiet conditions with above average temperatures are expected\nthrough the remainder of the week and into the weekend with high\npressure over the region. The clear skies and light winds at\nnight will make for efficient radiational cooling, with low\ntemperatures dipping into the low 30s and upper 20s again\ntonight. These large diurnal temperature shifts will continue\nwith the high pressure in place the next few days, however, as\nthe high shifts into the Atlantic over the next couple of days,\nweak southerly return flow should help keep the overnight lows a\nfew degrees higher. Finally, a very dry airmass will be\noverhead, but with the cool overnight temperatures and warm\nriver waters, expect at least river valley fog to still develop\nthe next couple of nights. \n\nThe next chance for rain isn't expected until Sunday, but there\nis still a lot of uncertainty with the synoptic setup this far \nout. A cold front will cross the region, which all guidance \nagrees on, but a sfc low tracking along or just off the East. \nIf the timing of the cold front is delayed a little longer, then\nthe coastal low could push a bit farther inland, and bring a greater\npotential for more rain into our area. If the sfc low is \nfarther off the coast, then there will be less rain with just \nthe potential for showers with the passing cold front.",
